---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { Laptop, Monitor, Keyboard, Mouse, Headphones } from 'lucide-astro';
---
<Base title="Uses" description="Tools I use for building products and writing code. The logos were 40% of the decision.">

  <div class="page-heading">
    <h1>Uses</h1>
    <p>Things I use every day and what powers my builds. Nobody asked, but the logos looked too good not to show off.</p>
  </div>

  <div class="tools-section">
    <p class="section-label">Things that power my life</p>

    <div class="tool-item">
      <div class="tool-icon">
        <img src="/logos/claude-color.svg" alt="Claude" />
      </div>
      <div class="tool-info">
        <span class="tool-name">Claude</span>
        <p>GPT ruins my frontend. Claude doesn't. My hair is still on my head.</p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="tool-item">
      <div class="tool-icon">
        <img src="/logos/codex-color.svg" alt="Codex" />
      </div>
      <div class="tool-info">
        <span class="tool-name">Codex</span>
        <p>My main models. Good for most tasks, and the limits don't feel like a punishment — unlike some other labs. Just not frontend.</p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="tool-item">
      <div class="tool-icon">
        <img src="/logos/cursor.svg" alt="Cursor" class="invert-dark" />
      </div>
      <div class="tool-info">
        <span class="tool-name">Cursor</span>
        <p>Moved from VS Code. Now I constantly switch between the two because Cursor has bugs, but VS Code is just meh. So here we are.</p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="tool-item">
      <div class="tool-icon">
        <img src="/logos/opencode-light.svg" alt="OpenCode" class="opencode-light" />
        <img src="/logos/opencode-dark.svg" alt="OpenCode" class="opencode-dark" />
      </div>
      <div class="tool-info">
        <span class="tool-name">OpenCode</span>
        <p>Best interface of any AI coding tool I've tried. No bugs, no weird jank. The OpenCode Go sub unlocking Chinese models is a nice bonus on top.</p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="tool-item">
      <div class="tool-icon">
        <img src="/logos/ghostty.svg" alt="Ghostty" />
      </div>
      <div class="tool-info">
        <span class="tool-name">Ghostty</span>
        <p>Terminal that's fast, native, and actually pleasant to look at.</p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="tool-item">
      <div class="tool-icon">
        <img src="/logos/notion.svg" alt="Notion" class="invert-dark" />
      </div>
      <div class="tool-info">
        <span class="tool-name">Notion</span>
        <p>I genuinely hate Notion. I've been trying to leave for two years. It just keeps working and I keep staying.</p>
      </div>
    </div>

  </div>

  <div class="tools-section">
    <p class="section-label">Things that power my apps</p>

    <div class="tool-item">
      <div class="tool-icon">
        <img src="/logos/nextjs.svg" alt="Next.js" class="nextjs-light" />
        <img src="/logos/nextjs-light.svg" alt="Next.js" class="nextjs-dark" />
      </div>
      <div class="tool-info">
        <span class="tool-name">Next.js</span>
        <p>Too lazy to switch. Moving on.</p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="tool-item">
      <div class="tool-icon">
        <img src="/logos/astro.svg" alt="Astro" />
      </div>
      <div class="tool-info">
        <span class="tool-name">Astro</span>
        <p>Used it for this very site. Ships zero JS by default, which is the only correct default.</p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="tool-item">
      <div class="tool-icon">
        <img src="/logos/expo-icon-2.svg" alt="Expo" class="invert-dark" />
      </div>
      <div class="tool-info">
        <span class="tool-name">Expo</span>
        <p>How I build mobile apps. I haven't touched a native Android or iOS bundle in years and I'd like to keep it that way.</p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="tool-item">
      <div class="tool-icon">
        <img src="/logos/convex.svg" alt="Convex" />
      </div>
      <div class="tool-info">
        <span class="tool-name">Convex</span>
        <p>Less boilerplate. Real-time built in. Still not sure how it works under the hood and I've made peace with that.</p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="tool-item">
      <div class="tool-icon">
        <img src="/logos/stripe (1).svg" alt="Stripe" />
      </div>
      <div class="tool-info">
        <span class="tool-name">Stripe</span>
        <p>The docs are good. That's it.</p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="tool-item">
      <div class="tool-icon">
        <img src="/logos/posthog.svg" alt="PostHog" class="posthog-light" />
        <img src="/logos/posthog-light.svg" alt="PostHog" class="posthog-dark" />
      </div>
      <div class="tool-info">
        <span class="tool-name">PostHog</span>
        <p>Tells you what your users are actually doing, not what you think they're doing. Humbling.</p>
      </div>
    </div>

  </div>

  {/* Hidden for now — "Things on my desk" section
  <div class="tools-section">
    <p class="section-label">Things on my desk</p>

    <div class="tool-item">
      <div class="tool-icon"><Laptop size={22} /></div>
